==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*4 [[Elder Sloth]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 0.67~1.67 seconds<sup>20f~50f</sup>.
*6 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 1~1.67 seconds<sup>30f~50f</sup>.
*3 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 0.67~1.67 seconds<sup>20f~50f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since cash is somewhat tight in this stage and the four Elder Sloths combine to be extremely aggressive pushers, attempting to kill the Elder Sloths can be a volatile strategy. Therefore, this stage revolves around stalling and preventing the Elder Sloths from overwhelming your defenses while dealing damage to the enemy base.

This stage is trivialized by [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]]. He's an excellent choice for stalling and chipping away at the enemy base, as his [[Omni Strike|Omnistrike]] allows him to snipe it from 850 range. However, it's crucial to keep the enemy stack alive before the Elder Sloths are behind the enemy base, because Cat God needs the Wall Doges as stepping stones to utilize his Omnistrike. To do so, simply spawn fast meatshields at the start of the round, like a [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] or a few [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cats]], to keep the Wall Doges stalled close to the base. After saving enough money, spawn Cat God and continue spamming meatshields to prevent the Elder Sloths from pushing into Cat God's range. Cat God's [[Knockback|knockback]] [[Multi-Hit|multi-hit]] will push back any advance the Elder Sloths have made and slowly chip away at the enemy base until you win the stage.

Strategies without Cat God involve keeping the Wall Doges alive while using snipers or super-backliners to chip the enemy base. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]] and [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] are attackers which fulfill these requirements, due to their range and blindspots. As with the above strategy, use fast meatshields to stall the Wall Doges at the start of the round. Keep the Wall Doges as close to the base as possible. Then, begin stacking your base-chipper units while continuing to stall the Wall Doges. The enemy base will slowly be whittled down until you've won the stage.

To speed up the process of chipping the enemy base, it's recommended to bring Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
Any units that can out-range, chip, or stall are recommended.

* [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]]: Capable of sniping the enemy base and preventing the Elder Sloths from pushing.
* [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]]: Chips the enemy base from across the stage with 1200 standing range. [[True Form]] allows for permanently slowing the Elder Sloths via [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)#:~:text=While he,easily.|Cyberstacking]].
* [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]]: Able to use the Wall Doges as stepping stones to chip the enemy base through his [[Long Distance|long distance]] attack.
* [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]: Effective at stalling the Wall Doges which spawn on stage startup.
* [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]: Similar niche to Green Shell Cat, but disposable and spammable. Can also be a reliable unit to stall the Elder Sloths.
* [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Reliably kills Those Guys which interfere with meatshielding.
* [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Quickly reaches the frontlines and prevents the Elder Sloths from pushing when the stack of meatshields is nuked.
* [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]]: Can chip at the Elder Sloths and enemy base since his 551 standing range exceeds them. Will easily die without perfect meatshielding.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Ubers capable of out-ranging the Elder Sloths can help with chipping the base or even killing the Elder Sloths.
* [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]]: Easily out-ranges the Elder Sloths at 850 standing range, chipping the base and heavily damaging every enemy on the field.
* [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]]: With [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] to [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] and 600 standing range, Aphrodite will quickly cripple the Elder Sloths from a comfortable range.
* [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Shares Aphrodite's 600 standing range and has massive damage to Traited. Additionally, they have a multi-hit hitbox with 1000 range which can chip the base.

